    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d68">

                <pb facs="0084" n="72" sameAs="frus:frus1939v01/pg72"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">762.71/43a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Minister in Rumania</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gunther</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-03-18T15:00:00-05:00">March 18, 1939—3
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>29. The <hi rendition="#italic">New York Times</hi> this morning carries an
                    article from London that “a virtual ultimatum had been issued by Germany to
                    Rumania to the effect that (1) Rumania should give up certain industries and (2)
                    should agree that her entire exports of grain, oil, lumber, cattle and
                    foodstuffs should go exclusively to Germany, in return for which Germany would
                    be ready to guarantee Rumanian territorial integrity.”</p>
                <pb facs="0085" n="73" xml:id="pg73"/>
                <p>Kennedy quotes the Rumanian Minister in London as confirming the general
                    substance but as saying that the demands were made a week or 10 days ago when
                        Wohlthat<anchor n="19" xml:id="d68-f1"/> was in Bucharest.</p>
                <p>The Rumanian Minister here<anchor n="20" xml:id="d68-f2"/> informs the Department
                    that knowledge of these demands has reunited all elements in Rumania and that
                        Maniu<anchor n="21" xml:id="d68-f3"/> and others are now subordinating
                    politics to national unity.</p>
                <p>Please telegraph such information as you can gain and analytic comments.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d68-f1" n="19" xml:id="d68-f1-content">
                <p>Helmuth Wohlthat, Economic Adviser to Marshal Goering.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d68-f2" n="20" xml:id="d68-f2-content">
                <p>Radu Irimescu.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d68-f3" n="21" xml:id="d68-f3-content">
                <p>Julius Maniu, founder of Rumanian National Peasant Party; Premier, 1928–31.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
